## 🔍 TROUBLESHOOTING

### Issue: "Module not found" Error

**Symptoms**:

```bash
ImportError: No module named '@project-name@'
```

**Diagnosis**:

```bash
which python  # Check if using venv
pip list | grep @project-name@  # Check if installed
```

**Solution**:

```bash
source .venv/@project-name@/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

### Issue: Tests Not Found

**Symptoms**:

```bash
python -m pytest
# No tests found
```

**Diagnosis**:

```bash
ls tests/  # Check test files exist
ls tests/test_*.py  # Check naming
```

**Solution**:

```bash
# Ensure test files start with test_
# Ensure test functions start with test_
# Run from project root
cd /path/to/@project-name@
python -m pytest
```

### Issue: Linting Failures

**Symptoms**:

```bash
ruff check src/
# Multiple errors
```

**Solution**:

```bash
# Auto-fix what can be fixed
ruff check --fix src/

# Format code
ruff format src/

# Check remaining issues
ruff check src/
```

### Issue: Virtual Environment Not Activating

**Symptoms**:

```bash
source .venv/@project-name@/bin/activate
which python  # Still shows /usr/bin/python
```

**Solution**:

```bash
# Recreate virtual environment
rm -rf .venv/@project-name@
python3 -m venv .venv/@project-name@
source .venv/@project-name@/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

